  clock: 2  # 5fa7
  nonce: 5fa7  # 5fa7
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-23 (in session), verbatim: \"i rule as you would pick\". The picks as put to the owner: (1) default values are not in the id: CHANGE the code (in TypeScript, changing \"x: number = 5\" to \"= 6\" must not give the function a new stable id); (2) pointer and reference marks: KEEP the code (only Go strips a leading *; Rust's &'a str is hashed as written); (3) Python visibility: KEEP the code (_name is recorded as private). The side question (does raising a PyPI grammar constraint bump SHAPE_ID_SCHEME) was mentioned to the owner as \"the current doc says no\" and was NOT put as a pick: it is not ruled. The v19 bump is approved (\"yes I approve the v19 bump\")."  # 5fa7
