  message: "Ruled by the owner 2026-11-23 (\"i rule as you would pick\": TypeScript default values OUT of the id; pointer and reference decorators KEEP the code; Python _name private KEEP the code) and built in PR #2354 (dev 39bef1108).\nRULE 1 RE-RUN on dev 39bef1108: export function f(x: number = 5) against = 6: stable ids DIFFERENT on dev 05ed6f5fe, SAME on 39bef1108 (a default hashes as \"= ...\" at any depth; having a default is still hashed). Builder's measure: knex 1, hocuspocus 13, nest packages 150 ids moved.\nRULES 2 AND 3: no code change; the spec states the code.\nNOT RULED: the item's side question (does raising a PyPI grammar constraint bump SHAPE_ID_SCHEME; docs/audits/0009 line 47 points at an ADR that no longer exists). Filed: WI-siror-bupaz-zofiz-jomam-jimim-komoh-vavad-sirar.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/closure/ (out_dev.txt = dev 39bef1108 after the merge, out_base.txt = dev 05ed6f5fe before it; repro trees t/, run.sh, q.py, presplit.py)."  # 9cc7
